      <div class="sg-panels">
        <section class="sg-panel" id="sg-panel-1" aria-labelledby="sg-h-1">
          <h2 id="sg-h-1" tabindex="-1"><span class="sg-hn">1</span> What you need</h2>
          <p>A shopping list for the whole setup. Tick what you have; the ticks stay in this browser only. <span class="sg-count" id="sg-need-count" aria-live="polite"></span></p>
          <ul class="sg-need">
            <li class="sg-item">
              <label class="sg-tick"><input type="checkbox" data-need="rytm" data-req="1" /><span><b>Analog Rytm MKII on OS 1.74</b> <em class="sg-req">Required</em></span></label>
              <p class="sg-why">Sidecar adds to the Rytm. The stock OS 1.74 file comes in the next step. A <b>computer</b> with a USB port and an SD card slot or reader (<b>Required</b>) patches and flashes the Rytm and writes the card.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sg-item">
              <label class="sg-tick"><input type="checkbox" data-need="pi" data-req="1" /><span><b>Raspberry Pi 5 (recommended) or Raspberry Pi 4 Model B (works), 4 GB or more</b> <em class="sg-req">Required</em></span></label>
              <p class="sg-why">One card boots both boards. The Pi 5 gives a lot more headroom (processor power for more voices and effects); Sidecar works on a Pi 4B too. <b>2 GB</b> of memory is the minimum; <b>4 GB or more</b> is recommended, so the unit is ready for future releases. See <a href={docs('introduction/hardware/')}>Hardware</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sg-item">
              <label class="sg-tick"><input type="checkbox" data-need="sd" data-req="1" /><span><b>A microSD card, 4 GB or more</b> <em class="sg-req">Required</em></span></label>
              <p class="sg-why">Its contents are replaced. The SD card image grows to fill the card on its first boot, up to 512 GiB (more is not used). A fast, larger card is better for the recorder. Dirtywave keeps a list of tested cards for its M8 tracker: <a href="https://dirtywave.com/pages/recommended-microsd-cards" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dirtywave's recommended microSD cards</a>. It is a list for another device, not tested by Sidecar, but it is a good place to start. See <a href={docs('using/storage/#the-sd-card-image-grows-to-fill-the-card-050')}>Storage</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sg-item">
              <label class="sg-tick"><input type="checkbox" data-need="psu" data-req="1" /><span><b>The official USB-C power supply</b> <em class="sg-req">Required</em></span></label>
              <p class="sg-why">Pi 4: the official 5.1 V 3 A supply. Pi 5: the official 27 W (5 V 5 A) supply. Plug it in directly, not through a hub. The Sidecar warns on the display and the web page when the supply is too weak. See <a href={docs('getting-started/install-pi/#raspberry-pi-5')}>Raspberry Pi 5</a> and <a href={docs('using/troubleshooting/')}>Troubleshooting</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sg-item">
              <label class="sg-tick"><input type="checkbox" data-need="cool" data-req="1" /><span><b>A heatsink or a fan</b> <em class="sg-req">Required</em></span></label>
              <p class="sg-why">The Pi runs the audio at full clock and slows itself down when it is too hot, and the sound can drop out. We recommend a <b>good passive heatsink</b> (a large aluminium heatsink case): it keeps the Pi cool and it is silent. A fan works too: on a Pi 5 the official Active Cooler or a case fan on the fan header, which the Sidecar drives itself (<a href={docs('using/pi5-fan/')}>AUTO, ON or OFF</a>). A case with its own display controls its own fan. See <a href={docs('using/troubleshooting/#keeping-it-cool')}>Keeping it cool</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sg-item">
              <label class="sg-tick"><input type="checkbox" data-need="usb" data-req="1" /><span><b>A short USB A-to-B cable</b> <em class="sg-req">Required</em></span></label>
              <p class="sg-why">From the Rytm's USB port to a USB-A port on the Pi, with a good cable like the one that comes with the Rytm. <b>No hub.</b> See <a href={docs('introduction/hardware/')}>Hardware</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sg-item">
              <label class="sg-tick"><input type="checkbox" data-need="display" /><span><b>A touch display</b> <em class="sg-opt">Optional</em></span></label>
              <p class="sg-why">Everything on the display is also on the Rytm and the web page, so you can go without one. Pick yours: it chooses the card image in step 5.</p>
              <fieldset class="sg-size sg-disp">
                <legend>Your display</legend>
                <label class="sg-choice"><input type="radio" name="sg-disp" value="800x480" checked /><span><b>HDMI 800x480 with USB touch</b><small>5" and 7" HDMI touch displays (Waveshare). Image: 800x480.</small></span></label>
                <label class="sg-choice"><input type="radio" name="sg-disp" value="1024x600" /><span><b>HDMI 1024x600 with USB touch</b><small>The GeeekPi 7" (EP-0194), a case for the Pi 4: tested on hardware. Image: 1024x600.</small></span></label>
                <label class="sg-choice"><input type="radio" name="sg-disp" value="800x480" /><span><b>DSI touch display</b><small>A 7" DSI display made like the official one (the OSOYOO 7" DSI V4.0 is confirmed on a Pi 4), or the official Raspberry Pi 7" Touch Display. On a Pi 5: the Raspberry Pi Touch Display 2, 7" (confirmed; the 5" is untested). Image: 800x480.</small></span></label>
                <label class="sg-choice"><input type="radio" name="sg-disp" value="800x480" /><span><b>No display</b><small>The Rytm and the web page are enough. Image: 800x480.</small></span></label>
              </fieldset>
              <p class="sg-why">Connect an HDMI display to the Pi's <b>micro-HDMI 0</b> (next to the power socket) before power-on. On a Pi 5 an HDMI display is scaled and slightly soft. See <a href={docs('using/display/#which-displays-work')}>Which displays work</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sg-item">
              <label class="sg-tick"><input type="checkbox" data-need="eth" /><span><b>An Ethernet cable</b> <em class="sg-opt">Optional</em></span></label>
              <p class="sg-why">For the web page at <code>sidecar.local</code> and for updates from your computer, without Wi-Fi. See <a href={docs('using/web-ui/')}>The web page</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sg-item">
              <label class="sg-tick"><input type="checkbox" data-need="split" /><span><b>A USB-C power and data splitter, for a Pi 5 with a computer</b> <em class="sg-opt">Optional, Pi 5 only</em></span></label>
              <p class="sg-why">Only if the Pi 5's USB-C port also goes to a computer (computer audio and MIDI, Overbridge through the Sidecar, or the web page over the USB-C cable). That port is also the Pi 5's power input, and a computer or hub port gives it only about 1.5 A: weak ports give under-voltage and resets. A splitter takes power from the 27 W supply and passes the data on to the computer; a header-pin power adapter does the same job. You do <b>not</b> need it for a plain setup: the Rytm has its own supply. See <a href={docs('using/usb-audio-midi/#powering-a-pi-5-with-a-computer-attached')}>Powering a Pi 5 with a computer attached</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="sg-item">
              <label class="sg-tick"><input type="checkbox" data-need="usbc" /><span><b>A USB-C data cable, for a Pi 5</b> <em class="sg-opt">Optional, Pi 5 only</em></span></label>
              <p class="sg-why">The Pi 5's USB-C port can carry its web page to your computer, with no Wi-Fi or Ethernet, as well as audio and MIDI. It is new in 0.5.0 (tried with a Mac). See the <a href={docs('release-notes/')}>release notes</a>.</p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="sg-panel" id="sg-panel-2" aria-labelledby="sg-h-2">
          <h2 id="sg-h-2" tabindex="-1"><span class="sg-hn">2</span> Back up and get the stock OS</h2>
          <p><b>Back up first.</b> Use Transfer (Elektron's tool for the Rytm) to back up your projects, kits, sounds and samples. Then you can always go back: see <a href={docs('getting-started/recovery/')}>Recovery to stock</a>.</p>
          <p>Download Elektron's OS 1.74 for the Analog Rytm MKII from Elektron's own support page, and unzip it. You need the file <code>Analog-Rytm_MKII_OS1.74.syx</code>. Sidecar does not host Elektron's file and never will.</p>
          <p class="sg-actions"><a class="sg-btn" href="https://www.elektron.se/support-downloads/analog-rytm-mkii" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Elektron: Analog Rytm MKII support page</a></p>
          <p class="sg-note">Already on OS 1.73, or want to stay there? See <a href={docs('getting-started/patch-and-flash/#which-os-174-or-173')}>which OS</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="sg-panel" id="sg-panel-3" aria-labelledby="sg-h-3">
          <h2 id="sg-h-3" tabindex="-1"><span class="sg-hn">3</span> Patch it in your browser</h2>
          <p>This is the Sidecar patcher. Leave the build on its default (the first in the list), drop the stock <code>Analog-Rytm_MKII_OS1.74.syx</code> on it, press <b>Patch</b>, then <b>Save .syx</b>. Your file never leaves your computer.</p>
          <iframe class="sg-frame" title="Sidecar patcher" src={`${base}/patcher/`} loading="lazy" height="780"></iframe>
          <p class="sg-note">The patcher does not show? <a href={`${base}/patcher/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open it in its own tab</a>. The hashes to check are on <a href={docs('getting-started/patch-and-flash/')}>Patch and flash the Rytm</a>. Never share the patched <code>.syx</code>: it holds Elektron's firmware.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="sg-panel" id="sg-panel-4" aria-labelledby="sg-h-4">
          <h2 id="sg-h-4" tabindex="-1"><span class="sg-hn">4</span> Flash the Rytm</h2>
          <ol class="sg-list">
            <li>Connect the Rytm to your computer with a USB cable, and open Transfer.</li>
            <li>Drop the patched <code>.syx</code> on Transfer and confirm on the Rytm.</li>
            <li>Wait for the Rytm to restart. After an OS upgrade it may also update its bootstrap at the first restart: <b>do not turn the power off then</b>.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="sg-tip"><b>Tip:</b> if the Rytm stays on <b>"Success! Rebooting"</b>, that is stock behaviour. Power cycle it.</p>
          <p class="sg-note">If the Rytm does not boot, hold FUNC while you power on for the STARTUP menu: <a href={docs('getting-started/recovery/')}>Recovery to stock</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="sg-panel" id="sg-panel-5" aria-labelledby="sg-h-5">
          <h2 id="sg-h-5" tabindex="-1"><span class="sg-hn">5</span> Make the SD card</h2>
          <fieldset class="sg-size">
            <legend>1. Pick your screen size</legend>
            {SIZES.map((z, i) => (
              <label class="sg-choice">
                <input type="radio" name="sg-res" value={z.res} checked={i === 0} />
                <span><b>{z.title}</b><small>{z.note}</small></span>
              </label>
            ))}
          </fieldset>
          <p class="sg-label">2. Download the image</p>
          <p class="sg-actions">
            <a class="sg-btn sg-btn-main" id="sg-dl" href={imageUrl('800x480')} data-base={`${RELEASE.repo}/download/${RELEASE.tag}/`} data-ver={RELEASE.version} download><span class="sg-dl-in"><b class="sg-dl-verb">Download</b> <span id="sg-dl-name" class="sg-dl-name">{image('800x480')}</span></span></a>
            <a class="sg-btn" id="sg-dl-sha" href={`${imageUrl('800x480')}.sha256`}>.sha256</a>
            <a class="sg-btn" href={releasePage} target="_blank" rel="noopener">The release page</a>
          </p>
          <p class="sg-note">Do not unzip it: Raspberry Pi Imager reads the <code>.img.zip</code> itself. The same images are in the release zip <code>sidecar-{RELEASE.version}.zip</code>. To check the download, in its folder run <code>shasum -a 256 -c</code> with the <code>.sha256</code> file beside it (Windows: <code>certutil -hashfile &lt;file&gt; SHA256</code> and compare).</p>
          <p class="sg-label">3. Write it with Raspberry Pi Imager</p>
          <ol class="sg-list">
            <li><a href="https://www.raspberrypi.com/software/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download and open Raspberry Pi Imager</a>. Use a microSD card of 4 GB or more: its contents are replaced.</li>
            <li><b>Choose Device:</b> a Raspberry Pi 4 or a Raspberry Pi 5. It does not matter: one image boots both.</li>
            <li><b>Choose OS:</b> scroll to the bottom, pick <b>Use custom</b>, and select the downloaded <code>.img.zip</code>.</li>
            <li><b>Choose Storage:</b> your SD card. Then <b>Next</b>.</li>
            <li>Asked about <b>OS customisation</b>, choose <b>No</b>. Its Wi-Fi, user and SSH settings are for Raspberry Pi OS and do nothing on Sidecar.</li>
            <li>Write, wait for the check, and eject the card.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="sg-note">balenaEtcher works too ("Flash from file", the same <code>.img.zip</code>). Or copy the card files by hand: <a href={docs('getting-started/install-pi/#make-the-sd-card')}>Install Sidecar</a>. On its first start the card grows to fill the SD card, which takes a moment, once.</p>
          <details class="sg-more">
            <summary>4. Optional: Wi-Fi, screen size and other settings (card config editor)</summary>
            <div class="sg-more-body">
              <p>After writing the card, open it on your computer (it shows as <code>SIDECAR</code>). Paste its <code>config.txt</code> and <code>cmdline.txt</code> into the editor, change what you need, and put the files it makes on the card in place of the card's own. Do it before you start the Pi. Everything runs in this page: nothing is sent. More: <a href={docs('getting-started/config-editor/')}>the card config editor</a>.</p>
              <ConfigEditor />
            </div>
          </details>
        </section>

        <section class="sg-panel" id="sg-panel-6" aria-labelledby="sg-h-6">
          <h2 id="sg-h-6" tabindex="-1"><span class="sg-hn">6</span> Connect</h2>
          <ol class="sg-list">
            <li>Put the SD card in the Pi.</li>
            <li>Connect the Rytm's USB port to a USB-A port of the Pi with a good, short USB A-to-B cable (like the one that came with the Rytm). <b>No hub.</b></li>
            <li>On the Rytm, set <b>SETTINGS &gt; SYSTEM &gt; USB CONFIG</b> to the <b>Overbridge</b> mode. That is the only Rytm setting Sidecar needs.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="sg-note">Optional: a touch display on the Pi's micro-HDMI 0 (<a href={docs('using/display/')}>which displays work</a>), and an Ethernet cable to your computer for the web page. Pi 5: <a href={docs('getting-started/install-pi/#raspberry-pi-5')}>what is different</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="sg-panel" id="sg-panel-7" aria-labelledby="sg-h-7">
          <h2 id="sg-h-7" tabindex="-1"><span class="sg-hn">7</span> Power up and play</h2>
          <ol class="sg-list">
            <li>Power the Pi with its official supply (5.1 V 3 A for a Pi 4B, 27 W for a Pi 5).</li>
            <li>After about <b>11 seconds</b> the Rytm shows the Sidecar's connect screen.</li>
            <li>Pick an <b>EXT machine</b> on a track and play it.</li>
            <li><b>Hold UP</b> to see every shortcut.</li>
            <li>Open <code>sidecar.local</code> in a browser, with the Pi on Ethernet, for the web page: <a href={docs('getting-started/install-pi/#first-boot-over-ethernet-sidecarlocal')}>pairing your browser</a>.</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="sg-label">Where next</p>
          <ul class="sg-links">
            <li><a href={docs('using/machines/')}>Voices and machines</a></li>
            <li><a href={docs('using/key-combinations/')}>Key combinations</a></li>
            <li><a href={docs('using/sequencer/')}>Sequencer and poly tracks</a></li>
            <li><a href={docs('using/troubleshooting/')}>Troubleshooting</a></li>
            <li><a href={docs('about/community/')}>Ask on Discord</a></li>
            <li><a href={docs('release-notes/')}>Release notes</a></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <nav class="sg-nav" aria-label="Step navigation">
          <button type="button" class="sg-btn" id="sg-prev">Back</button>
          <span class="sg-prog" aria-hidden="true"><i id="sg-bar"></i></span>
          <button type="button" class="sg-btn sg-btn-main" id="sg-next">Next</button>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="sg-foot">Full instructions: <a href={docs('getting-started/start-here/')}>Start here</a>. You can always go back to the stock OS: <a href={docs('getting-started/recovery/')}>Recovery to stock</a>.</p>
</div>

<style is:global>
  @font-face { font-family: 'Space Grotesk'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; font-display: swap; src: url('../assets/fonts/space-grotesk-latin-400-normal.woff2') format('woff2'); }
  @font-face { font-family: 'Space Grotesk'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 500; font-display: swap; src: url('../assets/fonts/space-grotesk-latin-500-normal.woff2') format('woff2'); }
  @font-face { font-family: 'Space Grotesk'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; font-display: swap; src: url('../assets/fonts/space-grotesk-latin-700-normal.woff2') format('woff2'); }
  @font-face { font-family: 'Doto'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; font-display: swap; src: url('../assets/fonts/doto-latin-600-normal.woff2') format('woff2'); }
  @font-face { font-family: 'Doto'; font-style: normal; font-weight: 900; font-display: swap; src: url('../assets/fonts/doto-latin-900-normal.woff2') format('woff2'); }

  /* the tokens of the Pi's web UI ("UV night"), scoped to this page; the light set is the same hues on a pale ground */
  .sg {
    --bg: #08071a; --card: #110f28; --border: #2c2950; --control-border: #6a64a0;
    --text: #eeedff; --label: #bdb9e8; --accent: #9a97ff; --warm: #ff7a5c; --focus: #ffd166;
    --on-accent: #08071a; --accent-tint: rgba(154, 151, 255, 0.12); --ok: #5fd08a;
    --card-texture: radial-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 1px, transparent 1px);
    --device: #1d1a42; --device-2: #2f2b58; --screen: #05040f; --screen-lt: #17153a; --pixel: #eeedff;
    --pcb: #2f8a5c; --sd: #5b8cf0;
    --radius-card: 0.875rem; --radius-control: 0.5625rem; --target: 2.75rem;
    --font-ui: 'Space Grotesk', system-ui, sans-serif; --font-dot: 'Doto', 'Space Grotesk', ui-monospace, monospace;
    /* the card config editor inside takes the page's colours */
    --sl-color-white: var(--text); --sl-color-gray-1: var(--text); --sl-color-gray-2: var(--label); --sl-color-gray-3: var(--label);
    --sl-color-gray-4: var(--control-border); --sl-color-gray-5: var(--border); --sl-color-gray-6: var(--card); --sl-color-black: var(--bg);
    --sl-color-accent: var(--accent); --sl-color-accent-high: var(--accent); --sl-color-accent-low: var(--accent-tint);
    font-family: var(--font-ui); color: var(--text); color-scheme: dark;
    max-width: 72rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  :root[data-theme='light'] .sg {
    --bg: #f3f2ff; --card: #ffffff; --border: #d3d0ee; --control-border: #5f59a6;
    --text: #14122e; --label: #4a4678; --accent: #4a45d6; --warm: #c2411f; --focus: #9a5b00;
    --on-accent: #ffffff; --accent-tint: rgba(74, 69, 214, 0.09); --ok: #1c7c45;
    --card-texture: none;
    --device: #c9c6ea; --device-2: #aeaad9; --screen: #0b0a22; --screen-lt: #ffffff; --pixel: #eeedff;
    color-scheme: light;
  }
  .sg *, .sg *::before, .sg *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
  .sg a { color: var(--accent); text-underline-offset: 0.15em; }
  .sg a:hover { text-decoration-thickness: 2px; }
  .sg code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.9em; background: var(--accent-tint); padding: 0.05em 0.35em; border-radius: 0.3em; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .sg :focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .sg-label { font-size: 0.8125rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--label); margin: 0 0 0.35rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .sg-head { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .sg-title { font-family: var(--font-dot); font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 5vw, 2.6rem); line-height: 1.1; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; color: var(--text); letter-spacing: 0; border: 0; }
  .sg-sub { margin: 0; max-width: 62ch; color: var(--label); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.55; }

  .sg-main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 17rem) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1.25rem; align-items: start; }
  .sg-rail { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; position: sticky; top: 1rem; }
  .sg-step { width: 100%; text-align: left; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.1rem 0.75rem; min-height: var(--target); padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem; cursor: pointer;
    background: var(--card); background-image: var(--card-texture); background-size: 5px 5px; color: var(--text); font: inherit; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-control); }
  .sg-step:hover { border-color: var(--control-border); }
  .sg-n { grid-row: span 2; width: 1.9rem; height: 1.9rem; border-radius: 50%; border: 1.5px solid var(--control-border); display: grid; place-items: center; font-family: var(--font-dot); font-weight: 900; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--label); align-self: center; }
  .sg-t { font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.25; }
  .sg-d { color: var(--label); font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.35; }
  .sg-step[aria-current='step'] { border: 2px solid var(--accent); background-color: var(--accent-tint); padding: calc(0.65rem - 1px) calc(0.75rem - 1px); }
  .sg-step[aria-current='step'] .sg-n { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); }
  .sg-step.done .sg-n { border-color: var(--ok); color: var(--ok); }

  .sg-work { display: grid; gap: 1rem; min-width: 0; }
  .sg-stage, .sg-panel, .sg-nav { background: var(--card); background-image: var(--card-texture); background-size: 5px 5px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-card); }
  .sg-stage { overflow: hidden; }
  .sg-stage svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 800 / 460; }
  .sg-stage .ui { font-family: var(--font-ui); }
  .sg-stage .px { font-family: var(--font-dot); font-weight: 900; fill: var(--pixel); }
  .sg-caption { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem 1rem; }
  .sg-cap-t { margin: 0; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .sg-cap-d { margin: 0.25rem 0 0; color: var(--label); max-width: 70ch; line-height: 1.5; }

  .sg-panel { padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem 1.25rem; }
  .sg-panel h2 { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 700; display: flex; gap: 0.6rem; align-items: baseline; border: 0; color: var(--text); }
  .sg-panel h2:focus { outline: none; }
  .sg-panel h2:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 4px; }
  .sg-hn { font-family: var(--font-dot); font-weight: 900; color: var(--accent); }
  .sg-panel p, .sg-panel li { line-height: 1.6; }
  .sg-panel p { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; }
  .sg-list { margin: 0 0 0.9rem; padding-left: 1.3rem; display: grid; gap: 0.3rem; }
  .sg-links { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; display: grid; gap: 0.2rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(14rem, 1fr)); list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sg-note { color: var(--label); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .sg-tip { border-left: 3px solid var(--warm); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--warm) 14%, transparent); padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 0 var(--radius-control) var(--radius-control) 0; }
  .sg-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .sg-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: var(--target); padding: 0.45rem 1rem; font: 700 0.9375rem var(--font-ui); text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; text-align: center;
    color: var(--text); background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--control-border); border-radius: var(--radius-control); max-width: 100%; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .sg-btn:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .sg a.sg-btn { color: var(--text); }
  .sg-btn-main, .sg a.sg-btn-main { background: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
  .sg-dl-in { display: block; text-align: center; }
  .sg-dl-verb { white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 700; }
  .sg-dl-name { display: inline-block; max-width: 100%; overflow-wrap: break-word; word-break: normal; font-weight: 500; }
  .sg-need { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .sg-item { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-control); padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem 0.2rem; }
  .sg-tick { display: flex; gap: 0.7rem; align-items: flex-start; min-height: var(--target); cursor: pointer; padding-top: 0.3rem; }
  .sg-tick input { width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem; margin-top: 0.15rem; accent-color: var(--accent); flex: none; }
  .sg-tick:has(input:focus-visible) { outline: 3px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .sg-tick:has(input:checked) b { text-decoration: line-through; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; opacity: 0.8; }
  .sg-req, .sg-opt { font-style: normal; font-size: 0.8125rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 0.05rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 999px; white-space: nowrap; margin-left: 0.25rem; }
  .sg-req { color: var(--on-accent); background: var(--accent); }
  .sg-opt { color: var(--label); border: 1px solid var(--control-border); }
  .sg-why { margin: 0 0 0.6rem 2rem; color: var(--label); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .sg-disp { margin: 0 0 0.6rem 2rem; }
  .sg-count { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; }
  .sg-btn[disabled] { opacity: 0.4; cursor: default; }
  .sg-frame { width: 100%; height: 780px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-control); background: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.8rem; }
  .sg-size { border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 1rem; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .sg-size legend { font-size: 0.8125rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--label); padding: 0; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .sg-choice { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: flex-start; min-height: var(--target); padding: 0.65rem 0.85rem; border: 1px solid var(--control-border); border-radius: var(--radius-control); cursor: pointer; }
  .sg-choice small { display: block; color: var(--label); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  .sg-choice input { margin-top: 0.3rem; accent-color: var(--accent); width: 1.1rem; height: 1.1rem; flex: none; }
  .sg-choice:has(input:checked) { border: 2px solid var(--accent); background: var(--accent-tint); padding: calc(0.65rem - 1px) calc(0.85rem - 1px); }
  .sg-choice:has(input:focus-visible) { outline: 3px solid var(--focus); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .sg-more { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-control); margin-top: 1rem; }
  .sg-more summary { cursor: pointer; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-weight: 700; min-height: var(--target); }
  .sg-more-body { padding: 0 1rem 1rem; }
  .sg-nav { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; }
  .sg-prog { flex: 1; height: 4px; background: var(--border); border-radius: 2px; overflow: hidden; }
  .sg-prog i { display: block; height: 100%; width: 0; background: var(--accent); }
  .sg-foot { margin: 1rem 0 0; color: var(--label); font-size: 0.9375rem; }

  /* the scene: a step fades in; the cable and the card move on a step change */
  .sg-stage .fade { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.3s ease; }
  .sg-stage .fade.on { opacity: 1; }
  .sg-stage .cable { fill: none; stroke: var(--label); stroke-width: 5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-dasharray: 600; stroke-dashoffset: 600; transition: stroke-dashoffset 0.6s ease; }
  .sg-stage .cable.on { stroke-dashoffset: 0; }
  #sg-sd { transition: transform 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.6, 0.05, 0.3, 1), opacity 0.3s ease; }

  /* JavaScript on: one panel at a time. Off: every panel shows, one under the other */
  .sg.sg-js .sg-panel { display: none; }
  .sg.sg-js .sg-panel.on { display: block; }
  .sg:not(.sg-js) .sg-nav, .sg:not(.sg-js) .sg-stage .sg-caption { display: none; }
  .sg:not(.sg-js) .sg-stage .fade { opacity: 1; }
  .sg:not(.sg-js) .sg-stage { display: none; }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .sg { padding: 0.9rem; }
    .sg-main { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .sg-rail { position: static; grid-auto-flow: column; grid-auto-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.35rem; }
    .sg-step { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); justify-items: center; padding: 0.4rem; }
    .sg-n { grid-row: auto; }
    .sg-t, .sg-d { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); white-space: nowrap; }
    .sg-step[aria-current='step'] { padding: calc(0.4rem - 1px); }
    .sg-frame { height: 860px; }
    .sg-panel { padding: 0.9rem; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .sg *, .sg *::before, .sg *::after { transition: none !important; animation: none !important; }
  }
</style>

<script>
  const root = document.getElementById('sg');
  if (root) {
    const N = Number(root.dataset.steps);
    const STEPS = JSON.parse(root.dataset.stepText || '[]');
    const rail = root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.sg-step');
    const panels = root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.sg-panel');
    const svg = root.querySelector('.sg-stage svg') as SVGSVGElement;
    const sd = root.querySelector('#sg-sd') as SVGGElement;
    const capK = root.querySelector('#sg-cap-k') as HTMLElement;
    const capT = root.querySelector('#sg-cap-t') as HTMLElement;
    const capD = root.querySelector('#sg-cap-d') as HTMLElement;
    const bar = root.querySelector('#sg-bar') as HTMLElement;
    const prev = root.querySelector('#sg-prev') as HTMLButtonElement;
    const next = root.querySelector('#sg-next') as HTMLButtonElement;
    let cur = 1;

    function show(n: number, user: boolean) {
      cur = Math.min(N, Math.max(1, n));
      svg.querySelectorAll<SVGElement>('[data-on]').forEach((el) => {
        el.classList.toggle('on', (el.getAttribute('data-on') || '').split(' ').includes(String(cur)));
      });
      // the SD card: by the laptop in step 4, in the Pi's slot from step 5
      sd.setAttribute('transform', cur >= 6 ? 'translate(532 352) rotate(90 14 17)' : 'translate(330 360)');
      capK.textContent = `Step ${cur} of ${N}`;
      capT.textContent = STEPS[cur - 1]?.t || '';
      capD.textContent = STEPS[cur - 1]?.d || '';
      rail.forEach((b, i) => {
        if (i + 1 === cur) b.setAttribute('aria-current', 'step'); else b.removeAttribute('aria-current');
        b.classList.toggle('done', i + 1 < cur);
      });
      panels.forEach((p, i) => p.classList.toggle('on', i + 1 === cur));
      prev.disabled = cur === 1;
      next.textContent = cur === N ? 'Done' : 'Next';
      next.disabled = cur === N;
      bar.style.width = `${(cur / N) * 100}%`;
      try { history.replaceState(null, '', `#step-${cur}`); } catch (e) { /* a sandboxed frame */ }
      if (user) {
        root.querySelector('.sg-stage')?.scrollIntoView({ block: 'start' });
        (root.querySelector(`#sg-h-${cur}`) as HTMLElement | null)?.focus({ preventScroll: true });
      }
    }

    rail.forEach((b, i) => b.addEventListener('click', () => show(i + 1, true)));
    prev.addEventListener('click', () => show(cur - 1, true));
    next.addEventListener('click', () => show(cur + 1, true));

    // the screen size picks the image
    const dl = root.querySelector('#sg-dl') as HTMLAnchorElement;
    const sha = root.querySelector('#sg-dl-sha') as HTMLAnchorElement;
    const name = root.querySelector('#sg-dl-name') as HTMLElement;
    const sceneImg = root.querySelector('#sg-scene-img') as SVGTextElement;
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="sg-res"]').forEach((r) =>
      r.addEventListener('change', () => {
        if (!r.checked) return;
        const file = `sidecar-${dl.dataset.ver}-sd-${r.value}.img.zip`;
        dl.href = `${dl.dataset.base}${file}`;
        sha.href = `${dl.dataset.base}${file}.sha256`;
        name.textContent = file;
        sceneImg.textContent = file;
      }),
    );


    // step 1: the ticks stay in this browser (localStorage may be missing: then they just do not stay)
    const needs = root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[data-need]');
    const count = root.querySelector('#sg-need-count') as HTMLElement | null;
    let saved: Record<string, boolean> = {};
    try { saved = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('sidecar-setup-need') || '{}'); } catch (e) { saved = {}; }
    const tally = () => {
      const req = [...needs].filter((i) => i.dataset.req);
      const done = req.filter((i) => i.checked).length;
      if (count) count.textContent = `${done} of ${req.length} required parts ticked.`;
    };
    needs.forEach((i) => {
      if (saved[i.dataset.need || ''] === true) i.checked = true;
      i.addEventListener('change', () => {
        saved[i.dataset.need || ''] = i.checked;
        try { localStorage.setItem('sidecar-setup-need', JSON.stringify(saved)); } catch (e) { /* no storage */ }
        tally();
      });
    });
    tally();
    // the display picked in step 1 picks the image in step 5
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="sg-disp"]').forEach((d) =>
      d.addEventListener('change', () => {
        const r = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(`input[name="sg-res"][value="${d.value}"]`);
        if (r && d.checked) { r.checked = true; r.dispatchEvent(new Event('change')); }
      }),
    );

    root.classList.add('sg-js');
    const m = /^#step-(\d)$/.exec(location.hash);
    show(m ? Number(m[1]) : 1, false);
    window.addEventListener('hashchange', () => {
      const h = /^#step-(\d)$/.exec(location.hash);
      if (h && Number(h[1]) !== cur) show(Number(h[1]), false);
    });
  }
</script>
